course: dictionary
lesson: 4339
title: Guard: one word, many jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word guard can be a noun (a person or thing) or a verb (an action). Check the sentence to see which. «Soldiers and guard-dogs stood past the castle gate.» Here a guard is a person or dog whose job is to protect the place.
explain: Guard can also mean to protect or watch something carefully. «Twelve pairs of ribs curve round from the spine like a cage, guarding the heart and lungs.» The ribs keep the heart and lungs safe, so guarding means protecting.
explain: Context gives you the meaning. «Think of a vegetable patch at school: once you plant beans, you have to stay, water them and guard them.» Try swapping in protect: «water them and protect them» still makes sense, so guard means protect.
fact: Guard can be a noun (a person or thing that protects) or a verb (to protect or watch carefully).
fact: A security guard protects shops and banks, and a lifeguard watches swimmers at pools and beaches.
fact: Shin guards and mouth guards protect sports players.
fact: «Be on your guard» means be careful, and «caught off guard» means surprised.
fact: On a British train, the guard is the person in charge.
exercise: «Toad is dragged over a drawbridge into a grim old castle, past soldiers and guard-dogs.» What is a guard-dog? | A dog that wins races | *A dog whose job is to protect a place | A dog that sleeps all day
exercise: «Twelve pairs of ribs curve round from the spine, guarding the heart and lungs.» What does guarding mean here? | *Protecting | Breaking | Counting | Dancing
exercise: What does «be on your guard» mean? | *Be careful | Be very loud | Fall asleep | Be happy about something
test: «In a meerkat group one meerkat stands on a rock as a guard while the rest dig for beetles.» Why does the meerkat stand on the rock? | To find beetles | To sleep in the sun | *To watch for danger | To look at the clouds
test: On a British train, who is the guard? | *The person in charge | A soldier in a tall hat | A passenger with a ticket
exam: In «Please guard my bag while I swim», what kind of word is guard? | adjective | *verb | noun | adverb
